# Accepted deviations from the KaSe tripwire. Format: file<TAB>pattern<TAB>why.
# A lost line = red check: its diff is the review mechanism.
scripts/check.sh	--fast|--host-only)	KaSe dialect: --host-only = standard --fast. Referenced by README, CLAUDE.md, seven docs/superpowers plans and .claude/settings.local.json
scripts/check.sh	--variant|--board)	KaSe dialect: --board = standard --variant. Same reference surface as the --host-only alias
scripts/check.sh	export IDF_CCACHE_ENABLE=1	project preamble: the 7 boards share most of their components, the cross-cache cuts the full build time
scripts/check.sh	command -v idf.py	a missing tool is not a regression: without the devshell, the build phase skips itself while announcing it, instead of a red indistinguishable from broken code (doctrine v0.12.0)
scripts/hooks/cc_session_start.sh	.kase-board	custom variant file, predates .tripwire-variant and referenced by .esp-dev.yml, CLAUDE.md and the kase-board-variant agent
scripts/check.sh	export IDF_COMPONENT_CHECK_NEW_VERSION=0	project preamble: the 2.2.2 component manager crashes at configure time by evaluating the registry's LVGL 9 manifests against an LVGL 8 sdkconfig (LV_USE_LIBJPEG_TURBO); the lock is authoritative, no network needed at build time
scripts/check.sh	mapfile -t ALL_VARIANTS	boards are discovered from boards/*/sdkconfig.defaults — a new board folder is its own registration (plan 2026-09-20 board-is-one-folder); the scaffold hard-codes the list
